e-parts":[[2024]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.4846249","published":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"subtype":"preprint"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,3,29]],"date-time":"2022-03-29T09:11:19Z","timestamp":1648545079994},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"Engineering Skill Development","issue":"5","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["jxu"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2020,5,5]]},"DOI":"10.37896\/jxu14.5\/115","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,5,10]],"date-time":"2020-05-10T12:47:53Z","timestamp":1589114873000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Encoding cross-domain sentiment by Stochastic Word Embedding"],"prefix":"10.37896","volume":"14","member":"24566","container-title":["Journal of Xidian University"],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2020,5,10]],"date-time":"2020-05-10T12:47:53Z","timestamp":1589114873000},"score":23.985168,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/open?id=1aW8Z_IhxJk73rvqcN1Cb0ncQsch2Pwp-"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2020,5,5]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"5","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2020,5,5]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.37896\/jxu14.5\/115","ISSN":["1001-2400"],"issn-type":[{"value":"1001-2400","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2020,5,5]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,10]],"date-time":"2026-06-10T15:00:47Z","timestamp":1781103647151,"version":"3.54.1"},"reference-count":37,"publisher":"IGI Global","isbn-type":[{"value":"9781668463031","type":"print"},{"value":"9781668463048","type":"electronic"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2022,6,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Sentiment analysis is used to detect the opinion\/sentiment expressed from the unstructured text. Most of the existing state-of-the-art methods are based on supervised learning, and therefore, a labelled dataset is required to build the model, and it is very difficult task to obtain a labelled dataset for every domain. Cross-domain sentiment analysis is to develop a model which is trained on labelled dataset of one domain, and the performance is evaluated on another domain. The performance of such cross-domain sentiment analysis is still very limited due to presence of many domain-related terms, and the sentiment analysis is a domain-dependent problem in which words changes their polarity depending upon the domain. In addition, cross-domain sentiment analysis model suffers with the problem of large number of out-of-the-vocabulary (unseen words) words. In this paper, the authors propose a deep learning-based approach for cross-domain sentiment analysis. Experimental results show that the proposed approach improves the performance on the benchmark dataset.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.4018\/978-1-6684-6303-1.ch008","type":"book-chapter","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,22]],"date-time":"2022-07-22T12:53:48Z","timestamp":1658494428000},"page":"157-173","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["A Deep Neural Network Model for Cross-Domain Sentiment Analysis"],"prefix":"10.4018","author":[{"given":"Suman","family":"Kumari","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Swami Keshvanand Institute of Technology, Management, and Gramothan, Jaipur, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Basant","family":"Agarwal","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Indian Institute of Information Technology, Kota, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0490-4413","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Mamta","family":"Mittal","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"G.B. Pant Government Engineering College, New Delhi, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"2432","reference":[{"key":"978-1-6684-6303-1.ch008.-1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Agarwal, B., Ramampiaro, H., Lan